{"author":{"id":"673e1e1b6fccff4da5524407c8a8cdc7caf18221aabb93f2bb36ffef5c2a95e8"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1779825259,"nonce":"V8peVYnGfaW6v6JDuGf/MkioK8E=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOSn4-Gc8AAAABDdWRd88AAAAGDMXJuw"},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779825432,"nonce":"ch95ua6rrYXAoNmZF9L48Ty5IFE=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOSn4-Gc8AAAABDxfjfA","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/karpenter-provider-rackspace-spot/issues/9#issuecomment-4548191100"},"message":"Confirmed in-cluster — Rackspace's pool API surfaces this as a \"Custom Metadata conflicts\" warning the moment we try to override those two labels:\n\n\u003e Pool 12d52faf-...: Label: custom label \"node.kubernetes.io/instance-type\" (value: \"ch.vs1.medium-hkg\") conflicts with existing node label (value: \"compute1-4\"); Label: custom label \"topology.kubernetes.io/region\" (value: \"hkg-hkg-1\") conflicts with existing node label (value: \"HKG\").\n\nGoing with approach (3) — stop fighting the CCM. As of next snapshot, `mergeLabels` no longer sets `node.kubernetes.io/instance-type` or `topology.kubernetes.io/region`. `karpenter.sh/*` and `karpenter.rackspace.com/*` are unaffected by the CCM (verified survives registration) so binding still works. `topology.kubernetes.io/zone` also survives and is required by the Karpenter scheduler, so that one stays.\n\nUser-visible consequence: workloads using `nodeSelector: node.kubernetes.io/instance-type=\u003cServerClass\u003e` won't target our nodes — they'd need to use `karpenter.sh/nodepool` or `karpenter.rackspace.com/*` instead. Worth documenting in the README. Re-opening with this issue tracking the documentation note + the future possibility of a label-mutating webhook if anyone really needs the override.","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779843997,"nonce":"QU05milGPDyHPCdjmGH9393nS64=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOSn4-Gc8AAAABDzjbQw","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/karpenter-provider-rackspace-spot/issues/9#issuecomment-4550351683"},"message":"Won't do — not worth the operational complexity.\n\nThe OpenStack CCM owns node.kubernetes.io/instance-type and topology.kubernetes.io/region post-registration. Fighting it requires a mutating webhook with cert management + a MutatingWebhookConfiguration + a ping-pong with the CCM every time it writes the labels back. A lot of moving parts for a cosmetic mismatch.\n\nThe labels Karpenter actually uses for binding (karpenter.sh/nodepool, capacity-type, registered, initialized) are not touched by the CCM. Karpenter's scheduler scores against InstanceType.Name from our provider, not the live Node label.\n\nUser-visible consequence: workloads using nodeSelector: node.kubernetes.io/instance-type=\u003cServerClass\u003e won't target our nodes. Documented expectation: use karpenter.sh/nodepool or karpenter.rackspace.com/* labels for affinity instead. README updated separately.","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779843998,"nonce":"WM/2shsX+xo6bPeUyIDWx/5Hv5o=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOSn4-Gc8AAAABDdWRd88AAAAGDVGCYA"},"status":2}]}